{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Show me, I pray, Your glory.</b> Our Sages, may their memory be for a blessing, said (Yalkut Shimoni 33:850) that he asked to see the reward of the commandments in the World to Come, which is called כָּבוֹד (glory), as it says (Proverbs 3:35) ״כָּבוֹד חֲכָמִים יִנְחָלוּ״ — 'The wise shall inherit glory.' ״וַיֹּאמֶר אֲנִי אַעֲבִיר כָּל טוּבִי עַל פָּנֶיךָ״ — 'And He said: I will cause all My goodness to pass over your face': this is the reward of this world, and this is the abundant good hidden away for the righteous; but in any event you cannot see all of it — only its edge shall you see. The reward of this world is designated by the term 'My back,' as something secondary that one casts behind him; but 'My face' — that is the reward of the World to Come, wherein the righteous behold the face of the Shechinah. So long as man is entangled in matter, he cannot see this, as it is written (Isaiah 64:3) ״עַיִן לֹא רָאָתָה״ — 'Eye has not seen' — and so forth. And concerning this He said: ״לֹא תוּכַל לִרְאוֹת אֶת פָּנָי״ — 'You cannot see My face' — for the face itself is the reward of the righteous, who derive pleasure from the light of His face, blessed be He. And this is what He said: ״וְרָאִיתָ אֶת אֲחֹרָי וּפָנַי לֹא יֵרָאוּ״ — 'You shall see My back, but My face shall not be seen.' And our Sages, may their memory be for a blessing, said (Berakhot 7a): He showed him the knot of the tefillin. For we find the name שַׁדַּי inscribed in the tefillin — namely שִׁי״ן יוֹ״ד from the front: a יוֹ״ד on the tefillin of the arm and a שִׁי״ן on the tefillin of the head — and this forms יֵשׁ, alluding to the reward of the World to Come, in which there is substantive reality and concreteness, as it is written (Proverbs 8:21) ״לְהַנְחִיל אוֹהֲבַי יֵשׁ״ — 'To cause those who love me to inherit יֵשׁ' — and so forth. And in His back, the דָּלֶ״ת appears in the knot of the tefillin, alluding to the reward of this world, which comes from the four directions of the world, as it is written (Genesis 28:14) ״וּפָרַצְתָּ יָמָּה וָקֵדְמָה״ — 'You shall spread abroad westward and eastward' — and so forth. So too the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses (Deuteronomy 3:27) ״עֲלֵה רֹאשׁ הַפִּסְגָּה וְשָׂא עֵינֶיךָ יָמָּה וָקֵדְמָה״ — 'Go up to the top of Pisgah and lift up your eyes westward and eastward' — and so forth, hinting to him that you will not be able to see anything but אֵת דְּבָתְרָי — 'that which is behind Me.' And so it is stated (Deuteronomy 34:1) ״וַיַּרְאֵהוּ ה׳ אֶת כָּל הָאָרֶץ עַד הַיָּם הָאַחֲרוֹן״ — 'And YHWH showed him all the land, up to the last sea' — and our Sages, may their memory be for a blessing, expounded (Sifrei Devarim 31:2): 'Up to the last day,' for the resurrection of the dead — but not up to and including it, for the reward of the resurrection of the dead YHWH did not show him, because he could not see it and grasp its essence at all. Therefore the word אֶת is used in connection with His back but not with His face, and as its Aramaic translation goes, ״יָת דְּבָתְרָי״ — that is, that which is secondary to Him and is outside of Him; but with regard to 'My face,' the word אֶת is not used, because the reward is not secondary to His face, blessed be He; rather, the light of His face is itself the very reward, as it is written (Isaiah 40:10) ״הִנֵּה שְׂכָרוֹ אִתּוֹ וּפְעֻלָּתוֹ לְפָנָיו״ — 'Behold, His reward is with Him, and His recompense before Him.'" "And this is the secret of the large עַיִן and דָּלֶ״ת in the verse ״שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — to say that the eye of man cannot see anything but דָּלֶ״ת, that is, the reward of this world. And akin to this is what we explained in our work עוֹלְלוֹת אֶפְרַיִם regarding what Rabbi [Yehudah HaNasi] said: 'The reason I am sharper than my colleagues is that I saw Rabbi Meir from behind; and had I seen him from in front, I would have been sharper still' (Eruvin 13b) — meaning that he grasped from him only those insights that were secondary to him, like something secondary that a person casts behind him; but had I grasped from the light of his face — that is, the core of his insights, which are designated by the term 'face' — I would certainly have been sharper still."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The Yalkut Shimoni citation includes a number; I read ש״צה as section 850 based on common numbering."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:27.294382747Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}